  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1240 AM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nTuesday - Saturday\n\nA flattened upper-level cutoff low continues to meander around the \nHudson Bay region to our north on Tuesday. Given the persisting \npattern, could see another embedded shortwave trough round the base \nof the longwave trough on Tuesday to bring additional shower and \nthunderstorm chances to our neck of the woods as suggested by the \nlatest global models. Similar to the pattern for the next two days, \nchances, strength, and location of this activity will depend on the \ntiming of the upper-level wave pairing with the low-level \nfront/instability gradient placement, which are subject to shift due \nto prior days convection/pattern. Nevertheless, as multiple NCAR AI \nNWP forecast ensembles suggests, the potential remains for some \nstorms for Tuesday.\n\nThen for the midweek, we begin to see the upper-level low begin to \nmove east-southeast into Quebec shifting the more active pattern \nfurther east. Northwesterly upper-level will to linger on the \nbackside of the departing trough and as a result looking at a drier \nstretch for the second half of the week as the GEFS and EPS \nensembles become more aligned with the upper-level ridge \nbeginning to build across the northern Plains and into the Upper \nMidwest into next weekend. \n\nTemps in the extended are trending toward normal through the first \nhalf of the week, but hints of near to even below normal temps \ntoward the end of the week. \n\nWagner",
